.Dd July 31, 2026
.Dt REBOOTCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rebootctl
.Nd validate rebootd policy and query shutdown state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm configtest
.Op Ar file
.Nm
.Cm status
.Nm
.Cm cancel
.Nm
.Cm reboot
.Op Ar delay-seconds
.Nm
.Cm reroot
.Op Ar delay-seconds
.Nm
.Cm shutdown
.Op Ar delay-seconds
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Cm configtest
validates the explicit-label allow list used by
.Xr rebootd 8 ,
defaulting to
.Pa /etc/rebootd.allow .
A missing or empty file is valid and means default deny for mutating
operations; status remains readable according to the service protocol.
.Cm status
uses
.Xr librebootctl 3
to report whether the service has initiated shutdown.
It performs no reboot or shutdown operation.
.Cm cancel
cancels the pending operation after the daemon has durably published its
cancellation notification.
It fails with
.Er ENOENT
when no operation is pending and remains subject to the daemon's exact-label
policy.
.Cm reboot ,
.Cm reroot ,
and
.Cm shutdown
request the corresponding privileged operation through
.Xr librebootctl 3 .
The default delay is 10 seconds.  An optional non-negative delay, bounded to
24 hours, may be supplied in seconds.
They return only after the daemon has accepted or rejected the request; an
accepted request may prevent the command from printing its confirmation if
the kernel transition completes first.
The daemon's exact-label policy remains authoritative.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr librebootctl 3 ,
.Xr rebootd 8
